# CLEAR environment contract (ENV-03)
#
# This file is the documented list of variables the app and its deploys need.
# It holds names and placeholders only — never a real value. `.gitignore`
# excludes every other `.env*` file precisely so this one can be committed.
#
# Local:  copy to `.env.local` and fill it in.
# Vercel: set the same names under Project Settings → Environment Variables for
#         Production, Preview and Development. Preview deploys read the Preview
#         scope, so a variable added to Production alone leaves every PR preview
#         without it.
#
# Only `VITE_`-prefixed names are inlined into the browser bundle, so only
# browser-safe values may carry that prefix. Server-side secrets are never
# listed here and never become Vercel browser variables:
#
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   CI / hosting secret storage (ENV-07)
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY           Supabase Edge Function secrets (GEN-02b)

# Supabase project URL. Browser-safe. Consumed by the client DATA-03 adds.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Supabase public anon key. Browser-safe by design — row-level security, not
# secrecy, is the boundary. Never the service-role key.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-key
